{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1786429287,"nonce":"e+Otmzyx6FXsgQZXcVPaI5gjuPw=","title":"SPEC names eight oto_* metrics that no collector constructs","message":"**What is wrong.** SPEC acceptance criterion 34, §H.8 and `api/openapi/openapi.yaml` name metrics that do not exist in the code. Grepping every registered collector found 35 `oto_*` metrics; these eight are named in the SPEC and constructed nowhere:\n\n- `oto_reconcile_divergence`\n- `oto_source_degraded_holds_total`\n- `oto_notification_suppressed_total`\n- `oto_delivery_attempts_total`\n- `oto_delivery_dead_total`\n- `oto_thread_recovered_total`\n- `oto_render_invalid_total`\n- `oto_check_violation_total`\n\n`oto_thread_recovered_total` is the interesting one: it SHIPPED, under the name `oto_thread_gap_recovered_total`. So AC-34 names a metric that exists with a different name, and the mismatch is mirrored into `web/src/api/generated/schema.d.ts`.\n\nConversely, three real and useful metrics are absent from AC-34's minimum list: `oto_thread_order_decisions_total`, `oto_thread_head_wait_seconds` and `oto_delivery_claim_lost_total`.\n\n**Why it matters.** An operator building alerts from the SPEC writes rules against metric names that will never produce a series, and a rule that never fires is indistinguishable from a system that is healthy. `docs/runbooks/` (added for d6d97de) documents the 35 that exist and carries a table of where each missing fact actually lives today — `source_health.divergence_count`, `notification_deliveries.status`, logs — rather than inventing pages, so the gap is currently documented but not closed.\n\n**Where.** `docs/design/SPEC.md` AC-34 (~:3654) and §H.8, `api/openapi/openapi.yaml`, `web/src/api/generated/schema.d.ts`, `docs/runbooks/README.md`.\n\n**Done when.** Each of the eight is either implemented or removed from the SPEC with a note saying which fact answers the question instead; `oto_thread_recovered_total` is reconciled with the shipped `oto_thread_gap_recovered_total` (rename one or the other, in both places); and the three real metrics missing from the list are added.","files":null}]}